positions.description:
Intern for the Scientific Networking division (ESnet) of the Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. 

Responsibilities:

- Design components of the new and improved On-Demand Secure Circuits and Advance Reservation System (OSCARS) used by ESnet to provision high-bandwidth circuits for research laboratories across the Department of Energy's network. Technologies used include: Java 8, the Spring framework, and Javascript. 

- Implement advanced networking features, particularly in the Path Computation Engine, enabling: 
  -- Shortest path constrained routing; 
  --  VLAN tag translation; 
  --  Provisioning of arbitrary sized link-disjoint path sets; 
  --  Non-mirrored forward and reverse paths in the MPLS layer; 
  --  Asymmetric bandwidth reservations in the forward and reverse directions; 
  --  Manycast request bundling to reserve K available paths out of a provided set;
  --  Waypoint path-finding to construct routes from a given list of nodes;
  --  Blacklist specification to avoid specific nodes;
  --  Bandwidth availability calculation along a path to enhance reservation process.

